  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Low byte of a 64-byte part in its page, indexed by part AND 3. With the page table $7f00 the source is $8000 + part*64."},
    {"at":4,"placement":"line","text":"The 9 sprite pointers of each frame buffer (VIC bank $c000): buffer 0 $01-$09 ($c040), 1 $0a-$12 ($c280), 2 $13-$1b ($c4c0), 3 $1c-$24 ($c700)."},
    {"at":40,"placement":"line","text":"Unused: the 4 pointer lists of shape_ptr_lists with columns 1 and 3 of each row exchanged. Nothing reads them; the mirrored copy changes the part order instead."},
    {"at":76,"placement":"line","text":"Address of the pointer list of each buffer in shape_ptr_lists: low bytes $3155, high bytes $3159."},
    {"at":84,"placement":"line","text":"Unused address table of shape_unused_mirror_lists ($3131, $313a, $3143, $314c): low bytes $315d, high bytes $3161. Nothing reads it."},
    {"at":92,"placement":"line","text":"Start of the 9 x 64 byte sprite buffer of each draw_buffer value: $c040, $c280, $c4c0, $c700. Low bytes $3165, high bytes $3169."},
    {"at":100,"placement":"line","text":"Builds the 9 sprites of fighter_frame of fighter X into its hidden buffer, then publishes the 9 pointers. It toggles draw_buffer (0/1 fighter 0, 2/3 fighter 1). Facing 1 uses the mirrored copy at $33e7. Callers: anim_step and the time-up code $15f6."},
    {"at":114,"placement":"line","text":"Normal copy: slot n gets part table n ($7ae0 + n*$48) at fighter_frame. Slots 0-2 are row 1, 3-5 row 2, 6-8 row 3, left to right."},
    {"at":136,"placement":"side","text":"Starts with the 9 pointers of this buffer"},
    {"at":147,"placement":"line","text":"Slot 0: part index from $7ae0. Index 0 = empty slot, pointer 0 (the blank sprite at $c000)."},
    {"at":159,"placement":"side","text":"Source page = $7f00[part] + shape_page_offset"},
    {"at":178,"placement":"side","text":"Copies 64 bytes"},
    {"at":188,"placement":"side","text":"Next 64-byte sprite in the buffer, also for an empty slot"},
    {"at":604,"placement":"line","text":"Copies the 9 new pointers to fighter_part_ptrs ($02+2n+X); the IRQ at line 0 reads them. Then it looks for fighter_frame in shape_row4_frames."},
    {"at":653,"placement":"side","text":"Not in the list: row4_ptr_* keep their old values"},
    {"at":659,"placement":"side","text":"Facing 1: entries 8-15"},
    {"at":678,"placement":"line","text":"The 8 frames of the jumps and somersaults (animations 5, 8, 9 and $0e) that have a floor shadow in sprite row 4."},
    {"at":686,"placement":"line","text":"Shadow sprite pointers of the left, middle and right column ($33b7, $33c7, $33d7): entries 0-7 facing 0, 8-15 facing 1. Pointers $55-$7b are fixed sprites at $d540-$deff; 0 is the blank sprite."}
  ],
